__mtLangPack('zh','gam',{"golden green":"金绿色","A grading table of a pearl farm in Rikitea":"Rikitea 一家珍珠养殖场的分级台","A jeweller orders a strand of <b>round, very shiny, peacock-green</b> pearls, all alike. Look at each pearl: <b>colour, shape and lustre</b>.":"一位珠宝商订购了一串<b>圆润、非常有光泽的孔雀绿</b>珍珠，每颗都要一样。仔细观察每颗珍珠：<b>颜色、形状和光泽</b>。","Into the strand":"穿进这串","Other tray":"另一个托盘","rings around it":"有环纹","bright lustre":"光泽明亮","dull lustre":"光泽暗淡","That one is {A}: beautiful, but not the colour ordered.":"这颗是{A}：很漂亮，但不是订购的颜色。","Baroque, not round: it goes to another order.":"巴洛克形，不是圆的：它要留给另一份订单。","It has rings around it: a lower grade.":"它有环纹：等级较低。","Its lustre is dull: the pearl does not shine like a mirror.":"它的光泽暗淡：这颗珍珠不像镜子那样闪亮。","Look again: round, bright and peacock green. That one is perfect for the strand!":"再看看：圆润、明亮、孔雀绿。这颗正适合穿进这串！","Into the strand.":"穿进这串。","Set aside for another order.":"留给另一份订单。","Into the other tray.":"放进另一个托盘。","Your strand of five peacock pearls is ready{A}. Pearls are graded by size, surface, lustre, shape and colour. Gambier pearls are known for their many colours, from silver grey to peacock green and aubergine; the cooler water of the lagoon helps.":"你的五颗孔雀绿珍珠串好了{A}。珍珠按大小、表面、光泽、形状和颜色分级。甘比尔群岛的珍珠以色彩丰富著称，从银灰色到孔雀绿和茄紫色；泻湖较凉的海水功不可没。","A pearl shell on the engraving table":"雕刻台上的一枚珍珠贝壳","At the school in Rikitea, students learn to engrave mother-of-pearl, nacre, from the oysters of the lagoon. <b>Follow the dots in order</b> to engrave a manu.":"在 Rikitea 的学校里，学生们学习雕刻珍珠母，也就是泻湖中珍珠贝的贝壳内层。<b>按顺序连接各个点</b>，雕刻一只 manu。","The red dot is next: a slip of the tool marks the shell for ever.":"下一个是红点：工具一滑，就会在贝壳上永远留下痕迹。","Your manu shines on the nacre. Rikitea has the only school in the islands that teaches nacre engraving; mother-of-pearl is about half of what the Gambier sells to the world.":"你的 manu 在珍珠母上闪闪发光。Rikitea 拥有群岛中唯一一所教授珍珠母雕刻的学校；珍珠母约占甘比尔群岛对外销售额的一半。","Inside the cathedral of Saint-Michel of Rikitea: the altar":"Rikitea 的 Saint-Michel 大教堂内部：祭坛","The cathedral of Saint-Michel in Rikitea was begun in {#1}, in coral stone. Its altar is decorated with <b>mother-of-pearl</b> from the lagoon. <b>Find the six pieces of nacre</b> that shimmer.":"Rikitea 的 Saint-Michel 大教堂始建于 {#1} 年，用珊瑚石建成。祭坛上装饰着来自泻湖的<b>珍珠母</b>。<b>找出六块闪闪发光的珍珠母</b>。","A nacre flower!":"一朵珍珠母花！","It shimmers like the inside of a shell.":"它像贝壳内壁一样闪闪发光。","Mother-of-pearl, from the oysters of the lagoon.":"珍珠母，来自泻湖中的珍珠贝。","Mass is starting and the choir sings. What do you do?":"弥撒开始了，唱诗班正在唱歌。你会怎么做？","Sit quietly at the back and listen":"安静地坐在后排聆听","Yes. Visitors are welcome at Sunday mass: dress modestly, stay quiet, and take photos only when it is over.":"对。欢迎游客参加周日弥撒：穿着要得体，保持安静，等弥撒结束后再拍照。","Walk around taking photos":"四处走动拍照","Not during mass: wait until it is over.":"弥撒期间不行：等结束后再拍。","Saint-Michel of Rikitea is often called the oldest monument of the Tahiti islands: {#1} m long, with two towers, built by Mangarevan stonemasons with missionary brothers, and restored in {#2}. The mission years were hard ones too: diseases and departures made the population fall sharply.":"Rikitea 的 Saint-Michel 常被称为 Tahiti 诸岛最古老的建筑：长 {#1} m，有两座塔楼，由 Mangareva 石匠和传教修士共同建造，并于 {#2} 年修复。传教的年代也很艰难：疾病和人口外流使人口急剧下降。","Pine trees":"松树","The trail starts among pines planted on the slopes.":"步道从山坡上种植的松林间开始。","Orange and lemon trees":"橙树和柠檬树","Then citrus trees: oranges and lemons are the Gambier’s fruit crop.":"接着是柑橘树：橙子和柠檬是甘比尔群岛的水果作物。","Tropical forest":"热带森林","Higher up, the tropical forest, ferns and moss.":"再往上是热带森林、蕨类和苔藓。","The trail up Auorotini, Mount Duff, and the lagoon below":"登上 Auorotini（Duff 山）的步道，以及山下的泻湖","Keep going, step by step.":"继续走，一步一步来。","With a guide you climb Auorotini, Mount Duff, about 440 m. {A}":"在向导的带领下，你攀登 Auorotini，即 Duff 山，海拔约 440 m。{A}","<b>The summit!</b> The whole lagoon lies below, ringed by its reef. The guide points: <b>where is {A}?</b> Tap it.":"<b>山顶到了！</b>整个泻湖就在脚下，四周环绕着礁石。向导指着问：<b>{A}在哪里？</b>点击它。","That is Mangareva, the island you are standing on!":"那是 Mangareva，就是你脚下这座岛！","Not that one. Look again at the shapes.":"不是那个。再看看岛屿的形状。","Exactly!":"完全正确！","You climbed Auorotini and named the islands of the lagoon. Mangareva means “the floating mountain”. In the old days, the sons of chiefs who would become kings were taken up to this sacred mountain for a time.":"你登上了 Auorotini，还说出了泻湖中各岛的名字。Mangareva 的意思是“漂浮的山”。古时候，将要成为国王的酋长之子会被带到这座圣山上住一段时间。","Yes! And now, where is {A}?":"对！那么，{A}在哪里？","Snorkelling in the lagoon of Aukena, over giant clams":"在 Aukena 的泻湖里浮潜，看砗磲","In the clear lagoon of Aukena you float over giant clams, <span>pahua</span>. Their soft mantles glow blue, green and purple. <b>Find them all</b> — look, but never touch.":"在 Aukena 清澈的泻湖里，你漂浮在砗磲 <span>pahua</span> 上方。它们柔软的外套膜闪着蓝色、绿色和紫色的光。<b>把它们全部找出来</b>——只能看，千万别碰。","A pahua: its mantle shimmers.":"一只 pahua：它的外套膜闪闪发光。","It closes slowly as your shadow passes.":"你的影子掠过时，它慢慢合上了。","Another one, wedged in the coral.":"又一只，嵌在珊瑚里。","Back on the beach, someone offers you a reef fish from the lagoon for lunch. What do you do?":"回到海滩上，有人请你午餐吃一条泻湖里的礁鱼。你会怎么做？","Ask the people of the island which fish are safe here":"问问岛上的人，这里哪些鱼可以安全食用","Yes. In the Gambier lagoon many reef fish carry ciguatera, a poison from tiny algae that cooking does not remove. Locals know which fish to eat.":"对。在甘比尔群岛的泻湖里，许多礁鱼带有雪卡毒，这是一种来自微小藻类的毒素，烹煮也无法去除。当地人知道哪些鱼能吃。","Grill it: cooking makes any fish safe":"烤了吃：煮熟后任何鱼都安全","No: cooking does not remove ciguatera.":"不对：烹煮无法去除雪卡毒。","Catch your own on the reef":"自己去礁石上抓","Riskier still: ask the islanders first.":"那就更危险了：先问问岛民。","You found six giant clams and knew to ask about the fish. The tiny alga behind ciguatera was first identified during an outbreak in the Gambier in {#1}: it is named Gambierdiscus after these islands. Pahua are protected: small ones may never be taken.":"你找到了六只砗磲，还知道要先问清楚鱼的情况。引起雪卡毒的微小藻类是 {#1} 年甘比尔群岛暴发中毒事件时首次被鉴定出来的：它以这些岛屿命名，叫 Gambierdiscus。Pahua 受到保护：小的绝对不能捕捞。","a basket of oranges":"一篮橙子","two breadfruit, mei":"两个面包果，mei","a fish from the reef":"一条礁鱼","Singers walking from house to house on Akamaru":"在 Akamaru 挨家挨户走唱的歌手们","At festival time, singers and dancers go from house to house: the <span>pupuraga</span>. At each door they sing, and the family gives fruit or fish. <b>Tap “Sing” when the rings meet</b>: four good notes to win each house.":"节日期间，歌手和舞者们挨家挨户地走：这就是 <span>pupuraga</span>。他们在每家门口唱歌，主人家会送上水果或鱼。<b>当圆环重合时点击“唱”</b>：唱好四个音就能赢得一户人家。","Sing!":"唱！","In tune!":"音准真好！","The family claps along.":"这家人跟着拍手。","Lovely voice!":"好美的歌声！","Three houses, three gifts: oranges, breadfruit and fish. In the Gambier, the pupuraga brings singers and dancers from door to door, and the peʻi dance, lively and graceful, is danced with chant. Sharing food is part of the song.":"三户人家，三份礼物：橙子、面包果和鱼。在甘比尔群岛，pupuraga 让歌手和舞者们挨家挨户地表演，而欢快优雅的 peʻi 舞则伴着吟唱。分享食物也是歌的一部分。","Off the beat. Wait for the rings to meet.":"没跟上节拍。等圆环重合再点。","A fishhook of pearl shell":"珍珠贝鱼钩","Carved from the inside of a pearl oyster, smooth and shiny.":"用珍珠贝的内壳雕成，光滑闪亮。","A basalt adze blade":"玄武岩锛子刃","Ground smooth, to shape wood for houses and canoes.":"磨得很光滑，用来加工建房子和造独木舟的木材。","Charcoal from a hearth":"炉灶里的木炭","Burnt wood can be dated: it tells when people cooked here.":"烧过的木头可以测定年代：它能告诉我们人们何时在这里做饭。","An archaeological dig on Taravai, laid out in squares":"Taravai 上划成方格的考古发掘现场","At Onemea on Taravai, archaeologists study a village where people lived more than a thousand years ago. You help them. <b>Brush each square gently</b>, layer by layer.":"在 Taravai 的 Onemea，考古学家们正在研究一个一千多年前有人居住的村落。你来帮助他们。<b>轻轻刷开每个方格</b>，一层一层地来。","sand only":"只有沙子","You have just uncovered something. What do you do?":"你刚刚发现了什么东西。你会怎么做？","Leave it exactly where it is, and call the archaeologist to record it":"把它原封不动地留在原处，叫考古学家来记录","Yes. Where a find lies is as important as the find itself. It is noted, photographed, and only then lifted by the team.":"对。发现物所在的位置和发现物本身一样重要。先做记录、拍照，然后才由团队取出。","Pick it up and put it in your pocket":"捡起来放进口袋","Never: finds belong to the island’s heritage, and moving them erases their story.":"绝对不行：出土物属于岛屿的遗产，移动它们会抹去它们的故事。","You uncovered a pearl-shell fishhook, a basalt adze and the charcoal of an old hearth, and left each one in place for the team. Onemea was lived in from around the year {#1}. Today only a handful of people live on Taravai.":"你发现了一枚珍珠贝鱼钩、一把玄武岩锛子和一处古老炉灶的木炭，并把每一件都留在原处交给团队。大约从公元 {#1} 年起，Onemea 就有人居住。如今 Taravai 上只住着寥寥几个人。","Snorkelling in the lagoon of Aukena, over giant clams set in the coral":"在 Aukena 的泻湖里浮潜，看嵌在珊瑚中的砗磲","In the clear lagoon of Aukena you float over giant clams, <span>pahua</span>, set in the coral heads. Their velvet mantles shimmer blue, green, purple and gold. <b>Find them all</b>: tap one and your shadow passes over it. Look, but never touch.":"在 Aukena 清澈的泻湖里，你漂浮在嵌在珊瑚丘里的砗磲 <span>pahua</span> 上方。它们天鹅绒般的外套膜闪着蓝、绿、紫和金色的光。<b>把它们全部找出来</b>：点击一个，你的影子就会从它上面经过。只看，绝不要碰。","Already seen: let it open again in peace.":"已经看过了：让它安安静静地再张开吧。","Your shadow passes: it pulls in its mantle and closes. It will open again in a moment.":"你的影子经过：它收起外套膜合上了壳。过一会儿它会再张开。","A pahua: the little pale dots along the mantle sense light and shadow.":"一只 pahua：外套膜边缘的小浅色点能感觉到光和影子。","Its colours come from tiny algae living in the mantle, which feed it with sunlight.":"它的颜色来自生活在外套膜里的微小藻类，它们利用阳光给它提供养分。","The round hole is its siphon: it breathes out filtered water through it.":"那个圆孔是它的水管：它通过水管排出过滤后的水。","Wedged in the coral: you could not lift it, and you must not try.":"牢牢嵌在珊瑚里：你搬不动它，也绝不能去试。","A big one, perhaps twenty years old. Pahua grow slowly.":"一只大砗磲，也许有二十岁了。Pahua 长得很慢。","That one is aubergine, a deep purple: beautiful, but not the colour ordered.":"那颗是茄紫，深紫色：很美，但不是订购的颜色。","That one is silver grey, pale and cool: beautiful, but not the colour ordered.":"那颗是银灰，浅而冷调：很美，但不是订购的颜色。","That one is pistachio, a yellow-green: beautiful, but not the colour ordered.":"那颗是开心果绿，黄绿色：很美，但不是订购的颜色。","That one is cherry, a red-brown: beautiful, but not the colour ordered.":"那颗是樱桃红，红棕色：很美，但不是订购的颜色。","That one is blue grey, a steel blue: beautiful, but not the colour ordered.":"那颗是蓝灰，钢蓝色：很美，但不是订购的颜色。","green with rose and blue lights":"绿色中泛着玫瑰色和蓝色的光","The grading room of a pearl farm in Rikitea: a black cloth on the table, a daylight lamp, sieves, a loupe and tweezers; through the window, the lagoon and the buoys of the farm":"Rikitea 一家珍珠养殖场的分级室：桌上铺着黑布，有一盏日光灯、几个筛子、一只放大镜和一把镊子；窗外是泻湖和养殖场的浮标","The harvest is washed and dried. <b>{#1}. Size.</b> Pearls are sorted by diameter through sieves: <b>tap the sieve</b> where each pearl stops. The grid shows the scale.":"收获的珍珠已经洗净晾干。<b>{#1}. 大小。</b>珍珠按直径用筛子分拣：每颗珍珠停在哪个筛子上，就<b>点击那个筛子</b>。网格显示的是刻度。","Semi-round":"近圆","Circled":"环纹","Baroque":"巴洛克","<b>{#1}. Shape.</b> Round is the rarest; more than four pearls in ten are baroque or semi-baroque. <b>Name the shape</b> of each pearl.":"<b>{#1}. 形状。</b>正圆最为稀有；十颗珍珠里有四颗多是巴洛克或半巴洛克。<b>说出每颗珍珠的形状</b>。","Almost round, but not quite: semi-round.":"几乎是圆的，但还差一点：近圆。","Flattened like a button.":"像纽扣一样扁平：扁圆形。","Pointed at one end: a drop.":"一端尖尖的：水滴形。","See the rings around it: circled.":"看它周围的一圈圈纹路：环纹。","No symmetry at all: baroque.":"完全不对称：巴洛克。","Perfectly round: the rarest.":"完美的正圆：最稀有的。","<b>{#1}. Surface and lustre, under the lamp.</b> <b>Tap the pearl to turn it</b> and look at every side, then give its grade: <b>A</b> clean with a mirror lustre (the top {#2} to {#3} %), <b>B</b> one or two small marks, <b>C</b> several marks, <b>D</b> marked all over or dull.":"<b>{#1}. 灯下看表面和光泽。</b><b>点击珍珠把它转过来</b>，看遍每一面，然后给出等级：<b>A</b> 级无瑕、有镜面般的光泽（最顶尖的 {#2}% 到 {#3}%），<b>B</b> 级有一两个小瑕点，<b>C</b> 级有几处瑕点，<b>D</b> 级满是瑕点或光泽暗淡。","Turn it first: the marks may be on the back.":"先把它转过来：瑕点可能在背面。","Look again: not a mark, and it shines like a mirror. Grade A.":"再看看：没有一个瑕点，而且像镜子一样闪亮。A 级。","One small mark that a setting could hide: grade B.":"一个小瑕点，镶嵌时可以遮住：B 级。","Several marks: grade C, the bulk of a harvest.":"几处瑕点：C 级，一次收获里大多数都是这一级。","Marked all over, and dull: grade D, for leather cords and cheaper pieces.":"满是瑕点，还很暗淡：D 级，用来做皮绳挂件和便宜的首饰。","[data-mm],[data-turn],[data-k]":"[data-mm],[data-turn],[data-k]","It falls straight through that one: try a finer sieve.":"它直接从那个筛子漏下去了：试试更细的筛子。","It will not pass: the holes are too small.":"它过不去：筛孔太小了。","Peacock: green with rose and blue lights.":"孔雀绿：绿色中泛着玫瑰色和蓝色的光。","A perfect match.":"完全匹配。","Your strand of five peacock pearls is ready. Each pearl was sized through the sieves, named by its shape, turned under the lamp and graded A to D, then matched by colour. Gambier pearls are known for their many colours, from silver grey to aubergine and peacock green: the cooler water of the lagoon helps. Before sale, every pearl must have at least {#1} mm of nacre.":"你的五颗孔雀绿珍珠串好了。每颗珍珠都经过筛子量出大小、按形状命名、在灯下转动并评定 A 至 D 级，最后按颜色配对。甘比尔群岛的珍珠以色彩丰富著称，从银灰到茄紫和孔雀绿：泻湖较凉的海水功不可没。出售前，每颗珍珠的珍珠层至少要有 {#1} mm 厚。","Your strand of five peacock pearls is ready, without a single mistake. Each pearl was sized through the sieves, named by its shape, turned under the lamp and graded A to D, then matched by colour. Gambier pearls are known for their many colours, from silver grey to aubergine and peacock green: the cooler water of the lagoon helps. Before sale, every pearl must have at least {#1} mm of nacre.":"你的五颗孔雀绿珍珠串好了，一次都没出错。每颗珍珠都经过筛子量出大小、按形状命名、在灯下转动并评定 A 至 D 级，最后按颜色配对。甘比尔群岛的珍珠以色彩丰富著称，从银灰到茄紫和孔雀绿：泻湖较凉的海水功不可没。出售前，每颗珍珠的珍珠层至少要有 {#1} mm 厚。","<b>{#1}. Colour.</b> A jeweller in Papeete orders a strand of five <b>peacock</b> pearls, all round, grade A, all alike. Here is the colour chip. <b>Tap the five that match.</b>":"<b>{#1}. 颜色。</b>Papeete 的一位珠宝商订购了一串五颗<b>孔雀绿</b>珍珠，全部正圆、A 级、颗颗一样。这是色卡。<b>点击匹配的五颗。</b>","a manu, the voyaging bird":"一只 manu，远航的鸟","a honu, the sea turtle":"一只 honu，海龟","a fai, the ray":"一条 fai，魟鱼","The engraving workshop of the Collège Saint-Raphaël in Rikitea: a bench under a lamp, a grinder, a micromotor, sandpaper and blue soap":"Rikitea 的 Collège Saint-Raphaël 雕刻工坊：灯下的一张工作台、一台砂轮机、一台微型电机、砂纸和蓝色肥皂","Thick, bright and whole: this one.":"又厚又亮又完整：就是这个。","Cracked: the burr would split it.":"有裂纹：磨头会把它磨裂。","Thin and dull at the edge: it would break.":"边缘又薄又暗：会碎的。","At the <b>Collège Saint-Raphaël</b> in Rikitea, students have learnt to engrave mother-of-pearl for twenty years. The shells come from the pearl farms: black-lip oysters, <span>pārau</span>. <b>{#1}. Choose the best shell:</b> thick, bright, and whole.":"在 Rikitea 的 <b>Collège Saint-Raphaël</b>，学生们学习雕刻珍珠母已有二十年。贝壳来自珍珠养殖场：黑唇珍珠贝，<span>pārau</span>。<b>{#1}. 选出最好的贝壳：</b>厚、亮、完整。","<b>{#1}. Cut the blank.</b> A round pendant is cut out of the shell with the saw. <b>Hold to cut</b>, and let go when the blade has gone all the way round, in the green zone.":"<b>{#1}. 切出坯料。</b>用锯子从贝壳上切下一个圆形吊坠。<b>按住切割</b>，等锯片绕完一整圈、到达绿色区域时松手。","Not all the way round: the blank is still attached.":"还没绕完一圈：坯料还连在贝壳上。","Too far: the blade bit into the pendant. Take another shell.":"过头了：锯片切进了吊坠。换一个贝壳。","<b>{#1}. Sand and polish.</b> First the grinder and the sandpaper, from coarse to fine, then a polish with blue soap: the reflections come out. <b>Hold to sand</b>, then <b>hold to polish</b> until the nacre shines.":"<b>{#1}. 打磨和抛光。</b>先用砂轮机和砂纸，从粗到细，再用蓝色肥皂抛光：光彩就显现出来了。<b>按住打磨</b>，再<b>按住抛光</b>，直到珍珠母发亮。","Hold: sand":"按住：打磨","Hold: polish":"按住：抛光","<b>{#1}. Draw the design</b> in pencil on the nacre. <b>Choose a motif.</b>":"<b>{#1}. 画出图案</b>，用铅笔画在珍珠母上。<b>选一种纹样。</b>","<b>{#1}. Engrave</b> with the micromotor: its tiny burr spins fast and leaves a fine groove. <b>Follow the pencil dots in order.</b> A slip marks the shell for ever.":"<b>{#1}. 雕刻</b>，用微型电机：它细小的磨头高速旋转，刻出一道细细的凹槽。<b>按顺序沿着铅笔点走。</b>手一滑，贝壳上就留下永久的痕迹。","The red dot is next: a slip of the burr marks the shell for ever.":"下一个是红点：磨头一滑，贝壳上就留下永久的痕迹。","Sand it smooth first, coarse then fine.":"先把它打磨光滑，先粗后细。","It shines like the inside of the shell.":"它像贝壳内壁一样闪亮。","They were not in the first plan: the brothers added them in {#1} and {#2}, when the church was nearly ten years old. Each one still carries its little spire.":"最初的设计里没有它们：修士们在 {#1} 年和 {#2} 年加建了它们，那时教堂已建成近十年。每座塔楼至今仍顶着自己的小尖顶。","Over the door, in Latin: “Who is like God?”, the meaning of the name Michael. The cathedral is {#1} m long, {#2} m wide and {#3} m high, the largest church in the South Pacific.":"门楣上的拉丁文：“谁能像上帝？”，这正是米迦勒这个名字的含义。大教堂长 {#1} m、宽 {#2} m、高 {#3} m，是南太平洋最大的教堂。","Coral stone and lime":"珊瑚石与石灰","The walls are blocks of coral limestone, covered with a plaster of coral lime. The stone was cut at Tauna, Tekava and Kouaku and brought by raft; Mangarevan masons built it with two lay brothers, Soulié and Costes, from {#1}.":"墙壁是一块块珊瑚石灰岩，外面抹着珊瑚石灰灰泥。石料在 Tauna、Tekava 和 Kouaku 开采，用木筏运来；从 {#1} 年起，Mangareva 石匠和两位平信徒修士 Soulié 与 Costes 一起建造了它。","Eighteen columns":"十八根立柱","Two rows of columns, cut from coral stone, hold up the vault.":"两排用珊瑚石凿成的立柱撑起拱顶。","A vault of bamboo":"竹子拱顶","The vault is three layers of mountain bamboo, crossed and lashed with coconut fibre, nape, then covered with coral lime. Inside, the cathedral was painted blue and white.":"拱顶由三层山里的竹子交叉叠放，用椰纤绳 nape 绑扎，再覆上珊瑚石灰。教堂内部漆成了蓝白两色。","The altar of nacre":"珍珠母祭坛","The altar is covered with engraved mother-of-pearl and set with black pearls from the lagoon: the work of Mangarevan craftsmen, like the nacre carvings all around the church.":"祭坛上覆盖着雕花珍珠母，并镶嵌着泻湖出产的黑珍珠：这是 Mangareva 工匠的作品，教堂四周的珍珠母雕刻也出自他们之手。","The crypt of Father Caret":"卡雷神父的墓室","Before the altar lies François Caret, one of the first missionaries of {#1}. The mission years brought the cathedral, but also hard times: illness from passing ships made the population fall sharply.":"祭坛前长眠着 François Caret，{#1} 年最早的传教士之一。传教的年代带来了这座大教堂，也带来了艰难的岁月：过往船只带来的疾病使人口急剧下降。","The cathedral of Saint-Michel of Rikitea: a white façade of coral stone with two towers, under the green hills of Mangareva; then its nave with two rows of columns, a blue vault and the altar of mother-of-pearl":"Rikitea 的 Saint-Michel 大教堂：珊瑚石砌成的白色正面和两座塔楼，背靠 Mangareva 青翠的山丘；然后是它的中殿，有两排立柱、蓝色拱顶和珍珠母祭坛","On the square of Rikitea stands <b>Saint-Michel</b>, begun in {#1} and finished in {#2}, restored in {#3}. <b>Tap the three glowing places</b> to look closer, then go in.":"Rikitea 的广场上矗立着 <b>Saint-Michel</b> 大教堂，始建于 {#1} 年，{#2} 年完工，{#3} 年修复。<b>点击三个发光的地方</b>仔细看看，然后走进去。","<b>Inside</b>, two rows of columns lead to the altar, under the blue vault. <b>Tap the four glowing places.</b> Speak softly: it is a church, and people pray here.":"<b>走进教堂</b>，蓝色拱顶下，两排立柱一直通向祭坛。<b>点击四个发光的地方。</b>请轻声说话：这是一座教堂，有人在这里祈祷。","Climb a tower for the view":"爬上塔楼看风景","No: the towers are not open, and this is a place of prayer.":"不行：塔楼不开放，而且这里是祈祷的地方。","You visited Saint-Michel of Rikitea outside and in: the two towers, the words over the door, the coral stone and lime, the eighteen columns, the bamboo vault, the altar of nacre and black pearls, and the crypt of Father Caret. Built from {#1} by Mangarevan masons with the Picpus brothers, it is the largest church in the South Pacific and was restored in {#2}. The same masons later went to Tahiti to build the cathedral of Papeete.":"你里里外外参观了 Rikitea 的 Saint-Michel 大教堂：两座塔楼、门楣上的文字、珊瑚石与石灰、十八根立柱、竹子拱顶、镶着珍珠母和黑珍珠的祭坛，还有卡雷神父的墓室。它从 {#1} 年起由 Mangareva 石匠和皮克普斯会修士共同建造，是南太平洋最大的教堂，并于 {#2} 年修复。后来，这些石匠又去了 Tahiti，建造了 Papeete 的大教堂。","The sign at the crossroads reads":"路口的指示牌上写着",". A shaded path follows a water pipe, past a small marae.":"。一条树荫小路沿着水管，经过一座小 marae。",", hand over hand, and let go at the top.":"，两手交替往上，到顶后松手。","More ropes on the steep hundred metres.":"陡峭的一百米上还有更多绳索。","blocks the way. The guide passes it":"挡住了去路。向导绕过它，走的是",", narrow and open to the wind: a drop on each side.":"，狭窄且迎风：两侧都是陡崖。","The trail up Auorotini, Mount Duff, from the sign at the crossroads through pines and scrub, past ropes and an overhanging rock, to the narrow summit ridge":"登上 Auorotini（Duff 山）的步道：从路口的指示牌出发，穿过松树和灌木丛，经过绳索和一块悬岩，直到狭窄的山顶山脊","With or without a guide, you climb":"有没有向导都行，你要攀登",", Mount Duff, {#1} m, the highest point of the Gambier: about {#2} hours there and back.":"，即 Duff 山，海拔 {#1} m，甘比尔群岛的最高点：往返约 {#2} 小时。","Walk on":"继续走","Right, up Mokoto":"向右，上 Mokoto","Left, for Auorotini":"向左，去 Auorotini","Mokoto is a fine short climb too, but not today: left, for Auorotini.":"Mokoto 也是一段不错的短程攀登，但今天不去：向左，去 Auorotini。","On the left":"左边","On the right":"右边","The left side drops away: the path goes round on the right.":"左边是陡坡：小路从右边绕过去。","Hold the rope":"抓住绳索","Too far: your hand slips off the end of the rope. Again.":"过头了：你的手从绳索末端滑脱了。再来。","Let go too soon: you slide back down. Hold on to the top.":"松得太早：你滑了下去。要一直抓到顶。","One step at a time: the next foothold is the glowing one.":"一步一步来：下一个落脚点是发光的那个。","Not that one. Look at the shapes again.":"不是那个。再看看那些形状。","A pearl-shell fishhook":"一枚珍珠贝鱼钩","A rotating hook, ground from the shell of a black-lip pearl oyster. Finished hooks, broken ones and half-made blanks were all found here: the fishermen made them on the spot.":"一枚旋转式鱼钩，用黑唇珍珠贝的贝壳磨制而成。这里出土了做好的鱼钩、断掉的鱼钩和做了一半的半成品：渔民们就在这里现场制作。","Fire-cracked stones and charcoal: an umu. The charcoal can be dated: this layer was lived in during the {#1}th and {#2}th centuries.":"被火烧裂的石头和木炭：一座 umu。木炭可以测定年代：这一地层在 {#1} 世纪和 {#2} 世纪有人居住。","Basalt flakes":"玄武岩石片","Hundreds of sharp flakes of dark basalt, struck from cores: the knives and scrapers of the camp. Some of the stone came from other islands.":"数百片锋利的深色玄武岩石片，从石核上打下来：这是营地的刀和刮削器。有些石料来自其他岛屿。","A coral file":"一把珊瑚锉","A branch of Acropora coral, worn smooth on one side: the file the fishermen used to shape and sharpen their shell hooks.":"一枝鹿角珊瑚（Acropora），一面已磨得光滑：渔民就用这把锉来打磨和磨尖贝壳鱼钩。","Seabird bones":"海鸟骨","Bones of petrels and shearwaters, broken for the marrow, from the first visits around the year {#1}. These birds nested here in thousands; most are gone from Mangareva today.":"海燕和鹱的骨头，为了取骨髓而被敲碎，来自大约公元 {#1} 年最早的造访时期。这些鸟曾成千上万地在这里筑巢；如今大多已从 Mangareva 消失。","Worked pearl shell":"加工过的珍珠贝","Pieces of pearl shell cut and ground: the blanks for hooks, waiting to be finished. One is still a rough half-moon.":"切割并打磨过的珍珠贝片：鱼钩的半成品，等着做完。有一片还是粗糙的半月形。","A rat bone":"一根鼠骨","The Pacific rat came in the first canoes. Its bones lie in the sand under the camp, with the seabirds it ate the eggs of.":"太平洋鼠是随着最早的独木舟来的。它的骨头躺在营地下方的沙子里，旁边就是被它偷吃过鸟蛋的海鸟。","Fish bones":"鱼骨","Bones of groupers, parrotfish and wrasses from the reef, with shells and land crabs: the menu of the camp.":"礁石上的石斑鱼、鹦嘴鱼和隆头鱼的骨头，还有贝壳和陆蟹：这就是营地的菜单。","Onemea bay on the south-west coast of Taravai: the reef, a small stream, and the sand dune at the head of the bay cut open by the archaeologists' trench, showing three layers of sand":"Taravai 西南海岸的 Onemea 湾：礁石、一条小溪，以及湾底的沙丘，被考古学家的探沟剖开，露出三层沙子","At <b>Onemea</b>, a sand dune at the head of a bay on the south-west coast of Taravai, archaeologists dug the oldest site known in the Gambier. You join the team. <b>{#1}. Peg out the trench</b>, {#2} m by {#3} m: tap the four corners in order.":"在 <b>Onemea</b>，Taravai 西南海岸一处海湾底部的沙丘上，考古学家发掘了甘比尔群岛已知最古老的遗址。你加入了他们的队伍。<b>{#1}. 用木桩标出探沟</b>，{#2} m 乘 {#3} m：按顺序点击四个角。","<b>{#1}. Trowel down</b>, unit by unit and layer by layer: <b>I</b> a thin dark soil, <b>II</b> grey sand full of charcoal, <b>III</b> yellow sand. <b>Tap a unit</b> to take off one layer. When something appears, record it before you lift it.":"<b>{#1}. 用手铲往下挖</b>，一个探方一个探方、一层一层地来：<b>I</b> 层是薄薄的深色土，<b>II</b> 层是满是木炭的灰沙，<b>III</b> 层是黄沙。<b>点击一个探方</b>挖掉一层。有东西露出来时，先记录再取出。","A land-crab burrow, with nothing in it. Fill it in and dig on.":"一个陆蟹洞，里面什么也没有。填上，继续挖。","Dig on":"继续挖","Something is showing in layer I.":"I 层有东西露出来了。","Something is showing in layer II.":"II 层有东西露出来了。","Something is showing in layer III.":"III 层有东西露出来了。","Lift it out":"取出来","Record it in place":"原地记录","Not yet: where a find lies, and how deep, is as important as the find. Photo, label and depth first.":"还不行：出土物在哪里、有多深，和出土物本身一样重要。先拍照、贴标签、记深度。","Now lift it out":"现在取出来","In order: the next corner is the glowing one.":"按顺序来：下一个角是发光的那个。","The trench is pegged and strung, three units of a metre.":"探沟已经打好木桩、拉好线，分成三个一米见方的探方。","A thin dark soil, roots, nothing else: layer I is modern.":"薄薄的深色土、树根，没别的：I 层是现代的。","Only sand.":"只有沙子。","<b>{#1}. Sieve the sand</b> from layer II through the screen: the small things hide in it. <b>Tap Shake</b> six times.":"<b>{#1}. 筛沙子</b>，把 II 层的沙子用筛网筛一遍：小东西都藏在里面。<b>点击“摇筛子”</b>六次。","Shake the sieve":"摇筛子","Three layers, one above the other. Which is the oldest?":"三个地层，一层叠一层。哪一层最古老？","Layer III, at the bottom, with the seabird bones":"最底下的 III 层，有海鸟骨的那层","Yes. Sand piles up: the deepest layer is the oldest. Its bird bones date from the first visits, around the year {#1}; layer II was the camp of the {#2}th and {#3}th centuries.":"对。沙子是一层层堆起来的：最深的地层最古老。它的鸟骨来自最早的造访时期，大约公元 {#1} 年；II 层是 {#2} 世纪和 {#3} 世纪的营地。","Layer I, on top":"最上面的 I 层","No: the top layer is the most recent. Layer I is modern soil.":"不对：最上面的地层是最新的。I 层是现代的土。","They are all the same age":"它们年代都一样","No: the layers were laid down one on another over centuries.":"不对：这些地层是几个世纪里一层一层叠起来的。","The sign at the crossroads reads <b>Mont Duff, Mokoto, Auorotini</b>. A shaded path follows a water pipe, past a small marae.":"路口的指示牌上写着 <b>Mont Duff, Mokoto, Auorotini</b>。一条树荫小路沿着水管，经过一座小 marae。","The path forks. The right branch climbs Mokoto, the left one Auorotini. <b>Which way?</b>":"小路分岔了。右边的岔路上 Mokoto，左边的去 Auorotini。<b>走哪边？</b>","The slope steepens: the first <b>rope</b>. <b>Hold to pull yourself up</b>, hand over hand, and let go at the top.":"坡变陡了：第一根<b>绳索</b>。<b>按住往上拉</b>，两手交替往上，到顶后松手。","Low scrub, then pines again, their needles soft underfoot, and wild raspberries along the path.":"低矮的灌木丛，然后又是松树，脚下的松针软软的，路边长着野树莓。","More ropes on the steep hundred metres. <b>Hold to pull up.</b>":"陡峭的一百米上还有更多绳索。<b>按住往上拉。</b>","A big <b>overhanging rock</b> blocks the way. The guide passes it <b>on the right</b>. Which side?":"一块大<b>悬岩</b>挡住了去路。向导绕过它，走的是<b>右边</b>。走哪边？","The forest ends. A short flat stretch, then the last climb to the ridge.":"森林到头了。一小段平路，然后是登上山脊的最后一段攀登。","<b>The ridge</b>, narrow and open to the wind: a drop on each side. <b>Tap each foothold in order</b>, one careful step at a time.":"<b>山脊</b>，狭窄且迎风：两侧都是陡崖。<b>按顺序点击每个落脚点</b>，小心地一步一步来。","a basket of oranges, picked from the trees behind the house":"一篮橙子，是从屋后的树上摘的","Akamaru at festival time: houses with orange trees along a path of coconut palms that leads to the blue and white church of Notre-Dame-de-la-Paix with its two different towers; the islet of Mekiro across the lagoon":"节庆时的 Akamaru：种着橙子树的房屋沿着一条椰林小路排开，小路通向蓝白相间、两座塔楼各不相同的 Notre-Dame-de-la-Paix 教堂；泻湖对面是 Mekiro 小岛","On Akamaru, about twenty people live by fishing, gardens and pearls. At festival time, singers and dancers go from house to house: the <span>pupuraga</span>. The leader sings a line (<b>gold</b> notes), the group answers (<b>red</b> notes). <b>Tap Sing when a red note reaches the mark.</b> Leave the gold ones to the leader.":"Akamaru 岛上住着约二十人，靠打鱼、种菜园和养珍珠为生。节庆时，歌手和舞者挨家挨户表演：这就是 <span>pupuraga</span>。领唱先唱一句（<b>金色</b>音符），众人再应答（<b>红色</b>音符）。<b>当红色音符到达标记时点击“唱”。</b>金色的留给领唱。","Three houses, three gifts: oranges, breadfruit and fish. In the Gambier, the pupuraga brings singers and dancers from door to door, for fruit, fish and today a little money; the peʻi, a dance found only here, is danced with chant. The path of palms leads to Notre-Dame-de-la-Paix, whose two different towers Father Laval wanted to recall Chartres: each year its statue of the Virgin, with a necklace of Tahitian pearls, goes to Rikitea at the end of July and comes home on {#1} August.":"三户人家，三份礼物：橙子、面包果和鱼。在甘比尔群岛，pupuraga 让歌手和舞者挨家挨户表演，换来水果、鱼，如今还有一点钱；peʻi 是只有这里才有的舞蹈，伴着吟唱而跳。椰林小路通向 Notre-Dame-de-la-Paix，Laval 神父希望它那两座不同的塔楼让人想起沙特尔大教堂：每年，戴着大溪地珍珠项链的圣母像在七月底前往 Rikitea，并于八月 {#1} 日回家。","Three houses, three gifts: oranges, breadfruit and fish, and you never sang over the leader. In the Gambier, the pupuraga brings singers and dancers from door to door, for fruit, fish and today a little money; the peʻi, a dance found only here, is danced with chant. The path of palms leads to Notre-Dame-de-la-Paix, whose two different towers Father Laval wanted to recall Chartres: each year its statue of the Virgin, with a necklace of Tahitian pearls, goes to Rikitea at the end of July and comes home on {#1} August.":"三户人家，三份礼物：橙子、面包果和鱼，而且你从没盖过领唱的声音。在甘比尔群岛，pupuraga 让歌手和舞者挨家挨户表演，换来水果、鱼，如今还有一点钱；peʻi 是只有这里才有的舞蹈，伴着吟唱而跳。椰林小路通向 Notre-Dame-de-la-Paix，Laval 神父希望它那两座不同的塔楼让人想起沙特尔大教堂：每年，戴着大溪地珍珠项链的圣母像在七月底前往 Rikitea，并于八月 {#1} 日回家。","Off the beat: wait until a red note sits in the ring.":"没踩准拍子：等红色音符落进圆环再点。","That was the leader’s line: let her sing, and answer on the red notes.":"那是领唱的部分：让她唱，你在红色音符上应答。","Lovely answer!":"应答得真好！","The whole street joins in.":"整条街都唱起来了。","<b>{A}.</b> {B} Photographed, labelled, depth noted.":"<b>{A}。</b>{B} 已拍照、贴标签并记录深度。","the front · tap to turn":"正面 · 点击翻转","the back · tap to turn":"背面 · 点击翻转","Grade {A}.":"{A} 级。","It stops at {A}.":"它停在 {A}。","each line: {#1} mm":"每格：{#1} 毫米","finds tray":"出土物托盘","<b>The summit</b>, with room for two to sit. The whole lagoon lies below inside its reef: the bays of Rikitea and Gatavake, Mokoto beside you, and the islands. The guide points: <b>where is {A}?</b> Tap it.":"<b>山顶</b>，只容得下两个人坐。整个潟湖在脚下，被礁石环绕：Rikitea 湾和 Gatavake 湾、身旁的 Mokoto，还有各个岛屿。向导指着问：<b>{A} 在哪里？</b> 点击它。","The family comes out with {A}. <span>Māuruuru!</span>":"这家人带着{A}走了出来。<span>Māuruuru!</span>"});
